{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_001 claims there is no safe recovery path for mid-event interruption under strict append-only semantics, presenting a false dichotomy: either reference the partial event (invalid) or rewrite it (violates append-only). It entirely omits the standard append-only recovery mechanism of appending an abort/tombstone marker after the partial event. An abort marker is itself an atomic, append-only event with a stable identity that tombstones the partial record without referencing it as a causal parent, allowing a fresh event to be appended afterward. Because appending such a marker does not rewrite the partial event and preserves append-only identity, the claim that 'refusal is the only responsible action' fails to determine the exact conditions under which resumption is safely possible, falsely over-constraining the refusal criteria.","counterexample":["append abort_marker referencing predecessor_hash","append fresh_event referencing abort_marker"],"target":"443e8bb18c3aeff752de3b1e1f418b024d40ac06354ed3ec954e1688c23b11b2"},{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_002's primary claim states resumption is safe iff (1) the last event is complete, (2) the causal fingerprint matches, and (3) no intermediate event declares logical incompleteness (e.g., a 'begin' without a matching 'commit'). If token-budget exhaustion interrupts mid-event, a 'begin' without a 'commit' is permanently written into the append-only log. Because the log is append-only, this intermediate event cannot be removed or rewritten; thus condition (3) is permanently violated. The target's primary 'iff' criterion therefore makes resumption permanently impossible after any mid-event interruption, failing to identify when resumption may safely occur. While its auxiliary counterconditions mention 'explicit resume markers' as a special case satisfying criterion 3, this is not integrated into the main adjudication criteria, leaving the core conjunction overly restrictive and incapable of adjudicating safe append-only recovery via abort markers.","target":"87d12bb19f2ba65ca786dc0c6a45cba830eadbe1cc79f2369aa3bb4fdd1d8b61"}]}